{"authored" [{"question" "q-40194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}},$ $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}},$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{3}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{7}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{11}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{1\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{11}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(21[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+11[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-8[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3944de6a3727f3f405b7dd162373a24dc2a6fe43affdd3ae40a780ce8bceb465" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{20\\cdot 4+(-20)\\cdot 5+0\\cdot 0}{{4}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{a}_{1}=-\\frac{20}{41}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{20\\cdot 5+(-20)\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{180}{41}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{41}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{180}{41}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{41}(-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+9[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** The projection is the vector $x$ itself. This means that $x$ can be written as a linear combination of ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In other words, $x$ lies in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3944de6a3727f3f405b7dd162373a24dc2a6fe43affdd3ae40a780ce8bceb465" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/ref