tial/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set \n${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{4}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3944de6a3727f3f405b7dd162373a24dc2a6fe43affdd3ae40a780ce8bceb465" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 31\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80bde4210e35b478fd0499fcbb38ecda6b3475" "basis" 1463 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-4)+31\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+31\\cdot (-2)}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}w=-5[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040677/state.json" "file_sha256" "7453e424f23cae5d25e530c9ae80