d}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set \n${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068823/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17857f99f1248b4b20894fdfb6976eb50fd23565097f524a0779507212390b1"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{4}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068823/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17857f99f1248b4b20894fdfb6976eb50fd23565097f524a0779507212390b1"} {"question" "q-39992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/dif